    "citations": [
      "WARSAW, POLAND—U.S. Secretary of Energy Chris Wright and Polish Energy Minister Miłosz Motyka today released the Partnership for Transatlantic Energy Cooperation (P-TEC) 2026 Chair Statement at the conclusion of the seventh P-TEC Ministerial and Business Forum in Warsaw, Poland.",
      "We recognize civil nuclear energy as essential to reliable power generation and long-term energy security, and support advancement of current and next-generation technologies, consistent with national priorities.",
      "We encourage investment in secure nuclear fuel supplies, workforce development, industrial capacity, and regulatory coordination to enable civil nuclear deployment at scale.",
      "We recognize the important contribution of firm, dispatchable generation, including coal, natural gas, and nuclear energy, to electricity affordability, grid reliability, and energy security, consistent with national priorities.",
      "We encourage the development of trusted supply chains for nuclear fuel, critical minerals, grid equipment, and other essential technologies, while welcoming private-sector and civil society engagement through the P-TEC Business Forum.",
      "We seek to strengthen long-term natural gas and liquified natural gas (LNG) partnerships, expand commercial opportunities, and improve access to diversified supplies across European markets in order to enhance energy security."
    ],
